              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "Depending on your context, **Chase Capital Services** (or **Chase Capital**) typically refers to one of three things:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Chase Auto Leasing & Car Titles (U.S. Automotive Context)\nIf you are looking at a car title, registration, or lease agreement, **Chase Capital Services** (often using various trust names like Chase Capital I, II, etc.) is the legal leasing entity used by **Chase Auto** (the auto financing arm of JPMorgan Chase). \n\n* **Why it is on your paperwork:** Chase is the private-label finance and lease provider for several automotive brands (such as Mazda, Subaru, Jaguar, and Land Rover). When you lease one of these vehicles, **Chase Capital Services** is legally listed as the **lessor (owner)** of the vehicle on state DMV records and titles.\n* **Common issues:** \n  * **Lease Buyouts:** If you are buying out your lease, you will need to work with Chase Auto to get a clean title transferred from \"Chase Capital Services\" to your name. \n  * **Moving Out of State:** If you move to another state while leasing, you will need a Power of Attorney (POA) from Chase to register the vehicle in your new state, as they are the titled owner.\n  * **Contact:** You can resolve these issues by logging into your Chase Auto account online or calling the Chase Auto customer service line at **1-800-336-6675**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Chase Capital Services Private Limited (India)\nIf you are looking for a corporate financial advisory firm in Asia, this is an independent company based in India.\n\n* **What it is:** Founded in 1997, it is an active, unlisted private financial services company registered in Chandigarh and headquartered in Mohali, Punjab. \n* **What they do:** They provide corporate financial consultancy, debt syndication (helping companies secure large loans), securitization, project consultancy, and currency/commodity trading services on recognized Indian exchanges.\n* **Key People:** Directed by Sunil Madan and Ajay Wadhwa.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Chase Capital (JPMorgan Chase Mid-Market Financing)\nIf you are looking for corporate investment/lending in the United States, **Chase Capital** is a specialized division of JPMorgan Chase.\n\n* **What it is:** Launched in 2007 and based in Chicago, this unit operates within Chase's commercial and middle-market banking division.\n* **What they do:** They provide subordinated debt (mezzanine financing) and equity investments to middle-market businesses to help them fund growth, navigate turnarounds, or execute recapitalizations. \n\n---\n\n*If you are trying to resolve an issue with a vehicle lease buyout, need a lien release, or are looking for contact info for one of these specific businesses, please let me know and I can provide more targeted details!*",
